WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.752
Wheel Spinner, Fortune Wheel, dice and Dicebreakers can organize prompts or turns.

2
00:00:05.952 --> 00:00:12.197
Bingo Caller, Bingo Card Generator and WebBingoMaker support bingo activity formats.

3
00:00:12.397 --> 00:00:15.472
Story Wheel can create a writing combination.

4
00:00:15.672 --> 00:00:18.798
Each tool needs a purposeful question around it.

5
00:00:18.998 --> 00:00:26.284
Ask every learner to think before the selected student responds, so a random turn does not become the only evidence

6
00:00:26.484 --> 00:00:27.533
you collect.

7
00:00:27.733 --> 00:00:34.239
A word search can help learners notice letter patterns, but finding a word does not establish its meaning.

8
00:00:34.439 --> 00:00:37.887
Follow with a definition, example or application.

9
00:00:38.087 --> 00:00:45.776
Coin Flipper and Dice Roller can generate probability observations; have students record outcomes and compare a

10
00:00:45.976 --> 00:00:47.799
prediction with the sample.

11
00:00:47.999 --> 00:00:53.051
A timer or scoreboard describes participation, not subject mastery.

12
00:00:53.251 --> 00:00:57.324
Before the activity, decide how you will respond to the evidence.

13
00:00:57.524 --> 00:01:01.322
An error in the underlying idea may need another worked example.

14
00:01:01.522 --> 00:01:06.369
A partially correct explanation may need targeted practice and feedback.

15
00:01:06.569 --> 00:01:09.933
A secure explanation may justify an extension.

16
00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:16.673
Pause and choose one utility, one aligned learner response and one decision you will make from that response.

